      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page ([[concepts/write-journal]]) describes the mechanism by which the guarded tool executor records and manages file state changes for potential rollback. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: Before any file is overwritten, the system records the file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If a run fails\u2014due to hitting a turn cap, encountering an unrecoverable error, or having all writes denied\u2014the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order, restoring previous file content or deleting newly created files.\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics**: This journal-based approach gives each run atomic write semantics (all changes succeed, or none do) without needing an actual database transaction\u2014the journal itself serves as the transaction log, kept in memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Query agent note**: The Query agent (used to query the wiki) doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write capability at all, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5372,
      "output_tokens": 255
    }
